        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hmm, there are probably also these items to consider. `expandcmd`'s behavior was introduced in PR #37729, but there don't seem to be any reports of issues so far. 🤔\n- [ ] [refactor: path.c cleanup](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/36112)\n  explore eliminating some functions that have overlapping purposes or are obsolete.\n  - eliminate path format transformations in `make_percent_swname`.\n    ref https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/39982#discussion_r3420216895\n  - drop MB_PTR_ADV in this file\n    ref https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40524#issue-4785783147\n- [ ] address lua-level normalization issues, like #23006, #33482, #33824.\n- [ ] address #16331\n- [ ] make filename modifiers respect logical root, ref #40545.\n- [ ] support editing device paths, like `:e //?/C:/foo/bar`\n  For now, `?` is treated as a wildcard. We could simply skip its root.\n  - may also support special dirs like `test.` in the future.\n- [ ] `expand` returns `\\`, while `expandcmd` may return `/`.\n  ```vim\n  echo expand('D:\\a\\foo\\*.md') \" => D:\\a\\foo\\b.md\"\n  echo expandcmd('D:\\a\\foo\\*.md') \" => D:/a/foo/b.md\"\n  ```\n- [ ] explore moving backslash conversion from `slash_adjust` to `:S` or `vim_strsave_shellescape`. This seems to be better for both consumers and maintainers.\n  ref https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/39155#discussion_r3545422138\n- [ ] collapse successive non-leading path sep\n  ref https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/39805#issuecomment-4808926196\n- [ ] explore preserving the drive letter across libuv path conversion. Maybe also look into how this interacts with LSP.\n  ref https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/39844#issuecomment-4586649330\n\nOh, I also need to enable some tests on Unix that were skipped in PR #39155.\nThe above items are a bit scattered. If you think any of them are higher priority, feel free to update the OP with them. :) cc @justinmk ",
